\id 3JN  John’s Third Letter 
\h 3 John 
\toc1 THE THIRD EPISTLE OF JOHN 
\toc2 3 John 
\toc3 3Jn 
\mt1 THE THIRD EPISTLE OF JOHN  
\c 1  
\p
\v 1 The \w elder\w* unto the \w wellbeloved\w* \w Gaius\w*, \w whom\w* \w I\w* \w love\w* \w in\w* the \w truth\w*.   
\p
\v 2 \w Beloved\w*, I \w wish\w* \w above\w* all \w things\w* \w that\w* \w thou\w* mayest \w prosper\w* \w and\w* be in \w health\w*, even \w as\w* \w thy\w* \w soul\w* \w prospereth\w*.  
\v 3 \w For\w* I \w rejoiced\w* \w greatly\w*, when the \w brethren\w* \w came\w* \w and\w* testified \w of\w* the \w truth\w* that is in \w thee\w*, even \w as\w* \w thou\w* \w walkest\w* \w in\w* the \w truth\w*.  
\v 4 I \w have\w* \w no\w* \w greater\w* \w joy\w* \w than\w* to \w hear\w* that \w my\w* \w children\w* \w walk\w* \w in\w* \w truth\w*.  
\v 5 \w Beloved\w*, thou \w doest\w* \w faithfully\w* \w whatsoever\w* thou \w doest\w* \w to\w* the \w brethren\w*, \w and\w* \w to\w* \w strangers\w*;  
\v 6 \w Which\w* have borne \w witness\w* of \w thy\w* \w charity\w* \w before\w* the \w church\w*: \w whom\w* if thou bring forward on their \w journey\w* \w after\w* a godly \w sort\w*, thou shalt \w do\w* \w well\w*:  
\v 7 Because \w that\w* \w for\w* \w his\w* \w name’s sake\w* they went \w forth\w*, \w taking\w* \w nothing\w* \w of\w* the \w Gentiles\w*.  
\v 8 \w We\w* \w therefore\w* \w ought\w* to \w receive\w* \w such\w*, \w that\w* we might \w be\w* \w fellowhelpers\w* to the \w truth\w*.   
\p
\v 9 I wrote \w unto\w* the \w church\w*: \w but\w* \w Diotrephes\w*, who loveth to have the \w preeminence\w* among \w them\w*, \w receiveth\w* \w us\w* \w not\w*.  
\v 10 \w Wherefore\w*, \w if\w* I \w come\w*, I will \w remember\w* \w his\w* \w deeds\w* \w which\w* he \w doeth\w*, prating \w against\w* \w us\w* \w with\w* \w malicious\w* \w words\w*: \w and\w* \w not\w* \w content\w* \w therewith\w*, \w neither\w* \w doth\w* he \w himself\w* \w receive\w* the \w brethren\w*, \w and\w* \w forbiddeth\w* them that \w would\w*, \w and\w* \w casteth\w* \add them\add* out \w of\w* the \w church\w*.   
\p
\v 11 \w Beloved\w*, \w follow\w* \w not\w* that which \w is\w* \w evil\w*, \w but\w* that which \w is\w* \w good\w*. \w He\w* that doeth \w good\w* \w is\w* \w of\w* \w God\w*: \w but\w* \w he\w* that doeth \w evil\w* \w hath\w* \w not\w* \w seen\w* \w God\w*.  
\v 12 \w Demetrius\w* hath good \w report\w* \w of\w* \w all\w* \add men\add*, \w and\w* \w of\w* the \w truth\w* \w itself\w*: \w yea\w*, \w and\w* \w we\w* \add also\add* bear \w record\w*; \w and\w* ye \w know\w* \w that\w* \w our\w* \w record\w* \w is\w* \w true\w*.   
\p
\v 13 I \w had\w* many \w things\w* to \w write\w*, \w but\w* I \w will\w* \w not\w* \w with\w* \w ink\w* \w and\w* \w pen\w* \w write\w* unto \w thee\w*:  
\v 14 \w But\w* I \w trust\w* I \w shall\w* \w shortly\w* \w see\w* \w thee\w*, \w and\w* we shall \w speak\w* \w face\w* \w to\w* \w face\w*. \w Peace\w* \add be\add* to \w thee\w*. \add Our\add* \w friends\w* \w salute\w* \w thee\w*. \w Greet\w* the \w friends\w* \w by\w* \w name\w*.
